{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Cursed_Tome","to":"Cursed Tome"},{"from":"Living_Wall","to":"Living Wall"},{"from":"Face_Trader","to":"Face Trader"},{"from":"Winding_Halls","to":"Winding Halls"},{"from":"The_Cleric","to":"The Cleric"},{"from":"Masked_Bandits","to":"Masked Bandits"},{"from":"Knowing_Skull","to":"Knowing Skull"},{"from":"Mysterious_Sphere","to":"Mysterious Sphere"},{"from":"Wheel_of_Change","to":"Wheel of Change"},{"from":"Ominous_Forge","to":"Ominous Forge"}],"pages":{"3204":{"pageid":3204,"ns":0,"title":"Cursed Tome","revisions":[{"revid":55408,"parentid":54577,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Cursed Tome\n|Image=Event-CursedTome.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Enchiridion}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Nilry's Codex}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Necronomicon}}\n{{E|Cursed Tome}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Read}}\n<blockquote>\n{{Frame|Continue}} {{TS|negative||Lose 1 HP.}}\n<blockquote>\n{{Frame|Continue}} {{TS|negative||Lose 2 HP.}}\n<blockquote>\n{{Frame|Continue}} {{TS|negative||Lose 3 HP.}}\n<blockquote>\n{{Frame|Take}} {{TS|positive||Obtain the book.}} {{TS|negative||Lose 10}} {{asc|15|(15)}} {{TS|negative||HP.}}\n* The book may be {{R|Enchiridion}}, {{R|Nilry's Codex}}, or {{R|Necronomicon}}. The player does not know which book they will get until after they choose {{Frame|Take}} and lose their HP.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Stop}} {{TS|negative||Lose 3 HP.}}\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n=== Practical Options ===\nBecause the player can choose to leave the event immediately and lose 0 HP instead of selecting {{Frame|Continue}} 3 times and then backing out with {{Frame|Stop}} while losing a total of 9 HP, there are really only 2 practical ways to navigate the event. The player can either commit to all the HP loss and obtain the book, or leave immediately to do nothing.\n\nFor simplicity, the event's options can be thought of in this way instead:\n* {{Frame|Read}}, then all 3 {{Frame|Continue}}, and finally {{Frame|Take}} {{TS|positive||Obtain the book.}} {{TS|negative||Lose 16}} {{asc|15|(21)}} {{TS|negative||HP.}} \n* {{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nIn an abandoned temple, you find a giant book, open, riddled with {{TS|purple|shake|cryptic writings.}} <br>\n\nAs you try to interpret the elaborate script, it begins to {{TS|blue|up|shift}} and {{TS|blue|up|morph}} into writing you are familiar with.\n</div>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Read}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nOdd. The book seems to be about an {{TS|gold||Ancient}} named {{TS|gold||Neow.}} <br>\n\nThis piques your interest, but you have a general feeling of {{TS|purple|up|malaise.}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe Ancient of Resurrection, {{TS|gold||Neow,}} was exiled to the bottom of the Spire. <br>\n\nYou feel compelled to read more, but your body begins to {{TS|negative|up|ache.}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nSeeking vengeance, {{TS|gold||Neow}} blesses outsiders, using them for her own purposes. <br>\n\nYou are starting to feel very {{TS|negative|up|weak and tired...}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThose resurrected by {{TS|gold||Neow}} remember only fragments of their past selves, cursed to fight for eternity. <br>\n\nAs you near the final page, your {{TS|negative|shake|old wounds begin to reopen!}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Take}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nUpon finishing the tome, you decide to take it with you. With proof in hand, will you retain your memories?\n</div></blockquote>\n{{Frame|Stop}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nWith incredible strain and willpower, you resist the trance of the tome and {{TS||shake|SLAM}} it shut. <br>\nYou turn and exit the temple, feeling {{TS|blue|up|drained...}}\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou exit, feeling a {{TS|purple|up|dark energy emanating}} from the book on the pedestal.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Tungsten Rod}} will reduce the HP lost for each instance of damage from the event's options. If the player selects {{Frame|Continue}} 3 times and then {{Frame|Take}}, {{R|Tungsten Rod}} reduces the total HP lost by 4 for a total of 12 {{Asc|15|(17)}} HP lost instead of 16 {{Asc|15|(21)}}.\n** If the player selects {{Frame|Stop}} instead of {{Frame|Take}}, {{R|Tungsten Rod}} reduces the total HP lost to 5 instead of 9.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding page turn SFX to Cursed Tome event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Seeds utilized for several events for consistent outcomes: Accursed Blacksmith, Cursed Tome, Scrap Ooze, N'loth.\n* '''Weekly Patch 16: Back to Work'''\n** Cursed Tome Event now uses reward screen for the earned book relic (optional pickup).\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3170":{"pageid":3170,"ns":0,"title":"Face Trader","revisions":[{"revid":55426,"parentid":54561,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Face Trader\n|Image=Event-FaceTrader.png\n}}\n{{E|Face Trader}} is a {{QueryLink|Events|shrine:Yes|shrine Event}} found in  [[Act 1]] and [[Act 2]]. This Event is the only way to obtain {{R|Cultist Headpiece}}, {{R|Face of Cleric}}, {{R|Gremlin Visage}}, {{R|N'loth's Hungry Face}}, and {{R|Ssserpent Head}}. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Touch}} {{TS|negative||Lose X HP,}} {{TS|positive||gain 75 {{Asc|15|(50)}} [[Gold]].}}\n* X is equal to 10% of the player's Max HP, rounded down.\n\n{{Frame|Trade}} {{TS|positive||50%: Good Face.}} {{TS|negative||50%: Bad Face.}}\n* Receive one of the following special [[Relics]]:\n** {{R|Face of Cleric}} ({{TS|positive||good face}})\n** {{R|Ssserpent Head}} ({{TS|positive||good face}})\n** {{R|Gremlin Visage}} ({{TS|negative||bad face}})\n** {{R|N'loth's Hungry Face}} ({{TS|negative||bad face}})\n** {{R|Cultist Headpiece}} (neutral face)\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou walk by an eerie statue holding several masks... <br>\nSomething behind you softly whispers, <br>\n{{TS||up|\"Stop.\"}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou swerve around to face the statue which is now facing you! <br>\nOn closer inspection, it's not a statue but a statuesque, gaunt man. Is he even breathing? <br>\n\n{{TS||up|\"Face. Let me touch? Maybe trade?\"}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Touch}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|\"Compensation? Compensation.\"}} <br>\nMechanically, he cranes out a neat stack of {{TS|gold||gold}} and places it in your pouch. <br>\n\n{{TS||up|\"What a nice face. Nice face.\"}} <br>\nWhile he touches your face, you begin to feel your life drain out of it! <br>\nDuring this, his mask falls off and shatters. Screaming, he quickly covers his face with all six arms dropping even more masks! Amidst all the screaming and shattering, you escape. <br>\n\nHis face was completely blank.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Trade}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|\"For me?}} {{TS||shake|FOR ME?}} {{TS||up|Oh yes.. Yes. Yes.. mmm...\"}} <br>\n\nYou see one of his arms flicker, and your face is in its hand! Your face has been swapped. <br>\n\n{{TS||up|\"Nice face. Nice face.\"}}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|\"Stop. Stop. Stop. Stop. Stop.\"}} <br>\n\nThis was probably the right call.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* The chances stated by the Event are inaccurate. The actual chances are 40% good face, 40% bad face, and 20% neutral face ({{R|Cultist Headpiece}}).\n** All 5 masks have the same probability of being chosen.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The masks held by the Face Trader in his portrait resemble other characters seen in the game.\n** From left to right, up to down: [[N'loth]], [[We Meet Again!|Ranwid]], [[The Cleric|Cleric]], the [[The Ssssserpent|Ssserpent]], [[Masked Bandits#Pointy|Pointy]], and [[Masked Bandits#Bear|Bear]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Face Trader event can no longer appear past Act 2.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Minor text cleanup for Face Trader event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Face Trader event will no longer give out duplicate relics on Endless mode.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** Improved Face Trader wording for top option to better reflect what happens.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Face Trader: It's a new event! This event shows up in any Act and can give you 1 of 5 relics exclusive to this event, we think it's facetastic.\n** Adding the Face Trader event.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3195":{"pageid":3195,"ns":0,"title":"Knowing Skull","revisions":[{"revid":55448,"parentid":54563,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Knowing Skull\n|Image=Event-KnowingSkull.png\n}}\n{{E|Knowing Skull}} is a {{QueryLink|Events|shrine:Yes|shrine Event}} found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It will only appear if the player has at least 13 HP; guaranteeing they can select at least 1 option and leave the event without dying.\n\n== Options ==\nThe following options are presented to the player until they decide to leave the event. X is equal to 10% of the player's Max HP (minimum of 6 HP) plus the number of times they have chosen that specific option ({{TS|negative||Lose 6 HP}}, then {{TS|negative||Lose 7 HP}}, then {{TS|negative||Lose 8 HP}}, etc.)\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|A Pick Me Up?}} {{TS|positive||Get a [[Potion]].}} {{TS|negative||Lose X HP.}} \n* A random [[Potion]] is immediately added to the player's left-most empty potion slot.\n* The player is able to select this option even if all their potion slots are full or if they possess {{R|Sozu}}. They still lose HP and this option's HP loss is still increased by 1 even though no potion is obtained.\n\n{{Frame|Riches?}} {{TS|positive||Gain 90 [[Gold]].}} {{TS|negative||Lose X HP.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Success?}} {{TS|positive||Get a}} {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless card}}. {{TS|negative||Lose X HP.}}\n* A random {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon&color:Colorless|Uncommon Colorless card}} is added to the player's deck.\n\n{{Frame|How do I leave?}} {{TS|negative||Lose X HP.}}\n* This event repeats until this option is chosen.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">You find yourself in an old, decorated chamber. In the center of the room, a large skull sits atop an ornate pedestal. As you approach, the skull {{TS|green|shake|bursts into flames}} and turns to face you.</div>\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<br>\n<br>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\"WHAT IS IT YOU SEEK? WHAT IS IT YOU OFFER?\" <br>\nIn sync with its final words, the door behind you {{TS||shake|slams shut.}}</div>\n<br><br>\n{{Frame|A Pick Me Up?}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"DRINK UP!\" <br>\nYou obtain a potion. <br>\n\n\"ANYTHING ELSE?\"\n</div>\n\nThe player is able to choose any of the [[#Options|Options]] again. {{Frame|A Pick Me Up?}} now costs 1 more HP than it did previously.\n</blockquote>\n\n\n{{Frame|Riches?}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"YOU MORTALS NEVER CHANGE. IT IS DONE.\" <br>\n{{TS|gold||Gold}} rains down on you! <br>\n\n\"ANYTHING ELSE?\"\n</div>\n\nThe player is able to choose any of the [[#Options|Options]] again. {{Frame|Riches?}} now costs 1 more HP than it did previously.\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Success?}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"PERHAPS THIS WILL HELP?\"\n\nYou obtain a card.\n\n\"ANYTHING ELSE?\"\n</div>\n\nThe player is able to choose any of the [[#Options|Options]] again. {{Frame|Success?}} now costs 1 more HP than it did previously.\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|How do I leave?}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"BEHIND YOU, MORTAL.\" <br>\nYou peek behind the skull. Surely enough, there is a door.\n</div>\n\nThe event ends, and the player is given the option to {{Frame|Leave}}.\n</blockquote>\n\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Bloody Idol}} can greatly increase the number of times the player can choose {{Frame|Riches?}} since they will heal 5 HP every time it gives them [[Gold]].\n* {{R|Tungsten Rod}} will reduce the HP lost by 1 every time an option is selected.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Knowing Skull event HP cost increases with each reward taken.\n\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Knowing Skull event can no longer give you a potion if you have the Sozu relic.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Events: Falling, Secret Portal, Knowing Skull, Golden Idol, and Scrap Ooze receive ambient BGM.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Knowing Skull HP cost minimum is set to 6 to prevent infinite gold with Bloody Idol.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Knowing Skull event now always asks for 10% of your Max HP instead of a set amount.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Knowing Skull event gets reworked. Die to your greed now.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Fixed Knowing Skull event options being ordered oddly after choosing the top option twice.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3182":{"pageid":3182,"ns":0,"title":"Living Wall","revisions":[{"revid":55453,"parentid":54554,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Living Wall\n|Image=Event-LivingWall.png\n}}\n{{E|Living Wall}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 1]]. \n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Forget}} {{TS|positive||Remove a card from your deck.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Change}} {{TS|positive||[[Transform]] a card in your deck.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Grow}} {{TS|positive||[[Upgrade]] a card in your deck.}}\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<i>\nAs you come to a dead-end and begin to turn around, walls {{TS||shake|slam down}} from the ceiling, trapping you!\n<br><br>\nThree faces materialize from the walls and speak.\n<br>\n{{TS|blue||\"Forget what you know, and I'll let you go.\"}}\n<br>\n{{TS|purple||\"I require change to see a new space.\"}}\n<br>\n{{TS|gold||\"If you want to pass me, then you must grow.\"}}\n</i>\n<br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Forget}}, {{Frame|Change}}, or {{Frame|Grow}} regardless of choice\n<br>\n<blockquote>\n<i>\nSatisfied, the walls in front of you merge back into the ceiling, leaving a path forward.</i>\n</blockquote></blockquote>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Fixed softlock caused if you can't remove cards in: Back to Basics, Cleric, and Living Wall events.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding ambient SFX for Living Wall event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 23: Testing Continues...'''\n** Living Wall event's transformed card is now seeded.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3158":{"pageid":3158,"ns":0,"title":"Masked Bandits","revisions":[{"revid":55642,"parentid":55310,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Masked Bandits\n|Image=Event-MaskedBandits.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Red Mask}}\n{{E|Masked Bandits}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. This Event and {{E|Tomb of Lord Red Mask}} are the only ways to obtain {{R|Red Mask}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Pay}} {{TS|negative||Lose ALL}} of your {{TS|gold||Gold.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Fight!}} \n* Starts a combat against [[#Bandits|the three bandits]] ({{M|Pointy}}, {{M|Romeo}}, and {{M|Bear}}). Upon winning, obtain regular card rewards, 25 - 35 [[Gold]], and {{R|Red Mask}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou encounter a group of bandits wearing large {{TS|red||red masks.}}\n<br>\n\"Hello, pay up to pass... a reasonable fee of {{TS||shake|ALL}} your {{TS|gold||gold}} will do! Heh heh!\"\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Pay}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nHehehe.. Thanks for the {{TS|gold||gold!}}\n<br>\nOh, I love {{TS|gold||gold.}} It's so nice.\n<br>\n{{TS|gold|up|shiny shiny}} chits they are!\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nHey {{TS|blue||Bear,}} hey!\n<br>\nThis guy gave us all his {{TS|gold||gold!}} What a sucker, right?<!-- This line does NOT change pronoun depending on the character (i.e. does not use \"she\" for Silent/Watcher, or \"it\" for Defect) -->\n<br>\nGet this, I just had to ask nicely. Who knew?!\n<br>\nI certainly didn't! What a chump!\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nGang, let's all have a laugh for this wondrous occasion!\n<br>\n{{TS||shake|Hahaah}}\n<br>\n{{TS||shake|Ho HOH}} {{TS||up|hoho!}}\n<br>\n{{TS||up|Hoh!}}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote>\nIf the player returns from the Map screen instead of progressing to the next floor, the event has extra dialogue:\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\"><br><br>\nOh? You're still here?\n<br>\nDid you overhear something? Didn't think so.\n<br>\n{{TS|red|shake|* snerk* }} {{TS||up|...loser....}} {{TS||shake|Hahaha}} {{TS||up|haaah}}\n</div></blockquote></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Fight!}}\n<blockquote>\n(No dialogue; the player enters combat with the [[#Bandits|Bandits]])\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Bandits ==\n=== Pointy ===\n----\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Pointy\n|Image  = Pointy.png\n|HP     = 30\n|AscHP  = 34\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Event\n}}\n{{Intents Table/start|Pointy}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Pointy Special\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (5\u00d72;{{Asc|2|6\u00d72}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nUses {{Int|Pointy|Pointy Special}} every turn.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n=== Romeo ===\n----\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Romeo\n|Image  = Romeo.png\n|HP     = 35-39\n|AscHP  = 37-41\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Event\n}}\n{{Intents Table/start|Romeo}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Mock\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Does nothing.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Agonizing Slash\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage. Applies (2;{{Asc|17|3}}) {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Cross Slash\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (15;{{Asc|2|17}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nAlways starts with {{Int|Romeo|Mock}}, then alternates between {{Int|Romeo|Agonizing Slash}} and {{Int|Romeo|Cross Slash}}.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, starts with {{Int|Romeo|Mock}}, then repeats the pattern of {{Int|Romeo|Agonizing Slash}}, {{Int|Romeo|Cross Slash}}, {{Int|Romeo|Cross Slash}}.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n=== Bear ===\n----\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Bear\n|Image  = Bear.png\n|HP     = 38-42\n|AscHP  = 40-44\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Event\n}}\n{{Intents Table/start|Bear}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Bear Hug\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies (-2;{{Asc|17|-4}}) {{BD|Dexterity}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lunge\n|Intent = DefendAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (9;{{Asc|2|10}}) damage. Gains 9 {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Maul\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (18;{{Asc|2|20}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nAlways starts with {{Int|Bear|Bear Hug}}, then alternates between {{Int|Bear|Lunge}} and {{Int|Bear|Maul}}.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Notes ==\n* Although the fight can be quite dangerous and offers a [[Relic]] reward, it does not count as an [[Elite]] combat for the sake of {{R|Preserved Insect}}, {{R|Sling of Courage}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Slaver's Collar}}.\n* If the player has {{R|Red Mask}}, the [[Act 3]] Event {{E|Tomb of Lord Red Mask}} will have an option to gain 222 [[Gold]] for free.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{M|Romeo}} appears in the Card art for {{C|Distraction}}.\n* {{M|Bear}} appears in the Card art for {{C|Rampage}} and {{C|A Thousand Cuts}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Ascension 17 Bear's  Dexterity debuff lowered from 5 to 4.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 24: Potions?!'''\n** Adding City Event: Red Masked Bandits\n\n{{EventNav}}\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3202":{"pageid":3202,"ns":0,"title":"Mysterious Sphere","revisions":[{"revid":55467,"parentid":54568,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Mysterious Sphere\n|Image=Event-Sphere.png\n}}\n{{E|Mysterious Sphere}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Open Sphere}} {{TS|negative||Fight.}} {{TS|positive||Reward: }} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{TS|positive||[[Relic]].}}\n* The player enters combat with the 2 {{M|Orb Walker|Orb Walkers}}. In addition to the {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]], the combat rewards also yield 45-55 [[Gold]], a normal card reward, and potentially a [[Potion]] just like a normal combat.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nJutting from the chaotic terrain around you, a bony sphere surrounds a mysterious glowing object within.<br>\nWhile you are curious what lies inside, you notice some sentries keeping an eye on it.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Open Sphere}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs soon as you strike the sphere, the sentries spring to life around you!\n</div>\n<br><br>\n{{Frame|Fight}}\n<br><br>\nThe sphere visually breaks open and the player enters combat with the 2 {{M|Orb Walker|Orb Walkers}}.\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nNo need to be greedy.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* Although the fight can be quite dangerous and offers a [[Relic]] reward, it does not count as an [[Elite]] combat for the sake of {{R|Preserved Insect}}, {{R|Sling of Courage}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Slaver's Collar}}.\n\n== Gallery ==\n{| style=\"float:left; margin:0 0 10px 10px;\"\n| [[File:SphereClosed.png|200px|thumb|The closed sphere.]]\n| [[File:SphereOpen.png|200px|thumb|The opened sphere.]]\n|}\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** The Mysterious Sphere event in Act 3 now uses the Double Orb Walker combat. (was Orb Walker and 2 Shapes)\n* '''Weekly Patch 31: Custom Mode'''\n** Clarified relic rarity on Mysterious Sphere event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks'''\n** Mysterious Sphere event enemies now attack in the correct order\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Minor wording improvements for the Mysterious Sphere event.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3197":{"pageid":3197,"ns":0,"title":"N'loth","revisions":[{"revid":55468,"parentid":54564,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=N'loth\n|Image=Event-Nloth.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|N'loth's Gift}}\n{{E|N'loth}} is a {{QueryLink|Events|shrine:Yes|shrine Event}} found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It will only appear if the player has at least 2 [[Relics]]. This Event is the only way to obtain {{R|N'loth's Gift}}.\n\n== Options ==\n'''Note:''' \"Relic A\" and \"Relic B\" will be randomly chosen from the player's currently held [[Relics]].\n<br><br>\n{{Frame|Offer: Relic A}} {{TS|negative||Lose this relic.}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a special relic.}}\n\n{{Frame|Offer: Relic B}} {{TS|negative||Lose this relic.}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a special relic.}}\n* Rewards the player with {{R|N'loth's Gift}}.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAn odd creature with a hunched back sprouting several tentacles is scrounging through a pile of trash and debris in front of you. As you approach, he shuffles towards you in a non-threatening manner.\n<br>\n\"N'loth hungry. Feed N'loth.\"\n</div>\n<br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Offer: Relic A}} or {{Frame|Offer: Relic B}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nHolding the {{TS|gold||relic}} out towards him, N'loth snatches it out of your hand with his tentacles, dislocates his jaw, and slurps down your offer in one quick gulp.\n<br>\nHe gives you a large, toothy grin as more tentacles appear from behind his cloak, these ones brandishing an impossibly neat looking box. He pushes it towards you until you take it.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou shake your head. N'loth hunches even further and sighs, then scuttles away.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* N'loth can pick Relics that activate their effects only upon being picked up, as well as used-up Relics.\n** For example, offering Relics like {{R|Mango}} or {{R|Old Coin}} will not remove the max HP or [[Gold]] granted by them, effectively removing the downside of {{R|N'loth's Gift}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|N'loth's Hungry Face}} from the {{E|Face Trader}} event references N'loth. There is no special dialogue if the player encounters N'loth while owning their face or if N'loth is traded their own face for {{R|N'loth's Gift}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding ambient sounds for N'Loth event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Seeds utilized for several events for consistent outcomes: Accursed Blacksmith, Cursed Tome, Scrap Ooze, N'loth.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Nloth's relic choices were alphabetical. Now it's random.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Nloth now appears in the City instead of the Exordium.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3063":{"pageid":3063,"ns":0,"title":"Ominous Forge","revisions":[{"revid":54536,"parentid":49493,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Ominous Forge\n|Image=Event-OminousForge.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Warped Tongs}} {{Small Card Infobox|Pain}}\n{{E|Ominous Forge}} is a shrine [[Event]] encountered in all [[Acts]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Forge}} {{TS|positive||Upgrade a card in your deck.}}\n<br><br>\n{{Frame|Rummage}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a special relic.}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed -}} {{C|Pain}}.\n* {{R|Warped Tongs}} - At the start of your turn, {{KW|Upgrade}} a random card in your hand for the rest of combat.\n* {{C|Pain}} - {{KW|Unplayable}}. While in hand, lose 1 HP whenever you play another card.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou duck inside a small hut. Inside you find what appears to be a forge. The smithing tools are covered with dust, yet a fire roars inside the furnace. You feel on edge...\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Forge}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou decide to put the forge to use and... <br>\n{{TS|gold|shake|CLANG CLAAANG CLANG!}} <br>\n...improve your arsenal!\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Rummage}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou decide to see if you can find anything of use. After uncovering tarps, looking through boxes, and checking nooks and crannies, you find a dust covered {{TS|gold|up|relic!}} <br>\n\nTaking the relic, you can't shake a sudden feeling of {{TS|negative|up|sharp pain}} as you exit the hut. Maybe you disturbed some sort of spirit?\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThere doesn't seem to be anything of use. You exit the way you came, the flames of the furnace casting {{TS|purple|up|eerie shadows}} on the walls inside the hut...\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* Internally called Accursed_Blacksmith.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3198":{"pageid":3198,"ns":0,"title":"The Cleric","revisions":[{"revid":55508,"parentid":54557,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Cleric\n|Image=Event-Cleric.png\n}}\n{{E|The Cleric}} is a {{QueryLink|Events|shrine:Yes|shrine Event}} found exclusively in [[Act 1]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}. It can only be encountered if the player has at least 35 [[Gold]]; enough to afford at least one of the options.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Heal}} {{TS|gold||35 [[Gold]]:}} {{TS|positive||Heal X HP.}}\n* X is equal to 25% of the player's Max HP, rounded down.\n\n{{Frame|Purify}} {{TS|gold||50}} {{Asc|15|(75)}} {{TS|gold||[[Gold]]:}} {{TS|positive||Remove a card from your deck.}}\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\nA strange blue humanoid with a golden helm(?) approaches you with a huge smile.\n\n{{TS||shake|\"Hello friend!}} I am {{TS|blue||Cleric!}} Are you interested in my services?!\" the creature shouts, loudly.\n\n{{Frame|Heal}}\n<blockquote><i>\nA warm golden light envelops your body and dissipates.\n\nThe creature grins. \"Cleric best healer. {{TS||shake|Have a good day!\"}}\n</i></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Purify}}\n<blockquote><i>\nA cold blue flame envelops your body and dissipates.\n\nThe creature grins. \"Cleric talented. {{TS||shake|Have a good day!\"}}\n</i></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><i>\nYou don't trust this {{TS|blue||\"Cleric\",}} so you leave.\n</i></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Cleric is also encountered in the {{E|Old Beggar}} event.\n* {{R|Face of Cleric}} from the {{E|Face Trader}} event references Cleric. There is no special dialogue if the player encounters Cleric while owning his face.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** You no longer run into The Cleric or Beggar events if you do not have enough gold.\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Fixed softlock caused if you can't remove cards in: Back to Basics, Cleric, and Living Wall events.\n* '''Weekly Patch 15: Surprise Patch'''\n** Cleric now shows and uses correct gold costs on Ascension 15.\n* '''Weekly Patch 14: Bullet Time'''\n** Cleric Event text improvements.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3070":{"pageid":3070,"ns":0,"title":"Wheel of Change","revisions":[{"revid":54550,"parentid":54549,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Wheel of Change\n|Image=Event-SpinTheWheel.png\n}}\n{{E|Wheel of Change}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other acts.\n{{Clear}}\n== Options ==\n<div style=\"float:right; display:flex; flex-direction:row; gap:10px; margin:0 0 10px 10px;\">\n[[File:SpinButton.png|100px|thumb|Spin Button.]]\n[[File:WheelArrow.png|100px|thumb|Wheel arrow.]]\n[[File:Wheel.png|250px|thumb|Wheel.]]\n</div>\n{{Frame|Play}}\n* Spin a wheel containing the following \"prizes\" (clockwise starting at 12 o'clock in the image):\n** Take 10% ({{Asc|15|15%}}) of your Max HP as damage.\n** Gain [[Gold]]\n** Gain a random [[Relic]]\n** Heal to full HP\n** Become Cursed - {{C|Decay}}\n** Remove a card from your deck.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou come upon a dapper looking, cheery gremlin. <br>\n\"It's time to spin the wheel! Are you {{TS||up|R E A D Y ?}} Of course you are!\"\n</div>\n<blockquote>\nWhen receiving a [[Relic]]\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Ah, a {{TS|green||gift!}} <br>\nEnjoy!\"\n</div></blockquote>\n\nWhen taking damage\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Uh oh! <br>\nYou lose!\" <br>\nYou spot him readying a shiv...\n</div></blockquote>\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou slash at the crazy gremlin but he's simply too quick! <br>\nHe gets you a few times with a crude shiv. <br>\n\"The price has been paid!!\" <br>\nand with that, both the gremlin and its wheel disappear in a puff of smoke.\n</div></blockquote>\n\nWhen obtaining [[Gold]]\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"You win some {{TS|gold||GOLD!}} <br>\nYAY!!!!\"\n</div></blockquote>\n\nWhen obtaining {{C|Decay}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Looks like you won a {{TS|purple||Curse!}} <br>\nThat's not good. <br>\nOh well! Better luck next time!\"\n</div></blockquote>\n\nWhen removing a card from your deck\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Ohh, the power of {{TS|negative|up|darkness...}} <br>\nChoose a card to remove from your deck!\"\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3190":{"pageid":3190,"ns":0,"title":"Winding Halls","revisions":[{"revid":55605,"parentid":54572,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Winding Halls\n|Image=Event-WindingHalls.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Madness}} {{Small Card Infobox|Writhe}}\n{{E|Winding Halls}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n<!-- Fix descriptions to be game accurate. Use TS template for colors. For percentages, replace with X and then in an indented bullet below, explain what X is equal to. -->\n{{Frame|Embrace Madness}} {{TS|positive||Receive 2 {{C|Madness}}.}} {{TS|negative||Lose X HP.}}\n* X is equal to 12.5% {{Asc|15|(18%)}} of the player's Max HP.\n\n{{Frame|Focus}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed - {{C|Writhe}}.}} {{TS|positive||Heal X HP.}}\n* X is equal to 25% {{Asc|15|(20%)}} of the player's Max HP.\n\n{{Frame|Retrace Your Steps}} {{TS|negative||Lose X Max HP.}}\n* X is equal to 5% of the player's Max HP.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you slowly make your way up the twisting pathways, you constantly find yourself losing your way as the walls and ground seem to inexplicably shift before your eyes<br>\n<br>\nThe constant {{TS|purple|up|whispering voices}} in the back of your head aren't helping things either.\n</div>\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|...}}\n<br>\n<br>\nPassing by a structure you are certain you have previously seen you start to question if you are going insane, or if the impossible geography of this place is starting to get to you. You need to change something, and soon.<br>\n<br>\nThat's what the {{TS|purple|up|voices}} say anyway, and why would they lie?\n\n{{Frame|Embrace Madness}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nSomething in you cracks.<br>\n<br>\nOnly the truly mad can understand a place like this, so you give into the chattering voices and continue on with a {{TS|purple|up|\"new\"}} perspective.<br>\nThings do seem to make so much more sense now.\n</div> </blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Focus}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you take a moment to stop and carefully observe the undulating landscape around you, the hint of a pattern starts to emerge from within the randomness. Whenever the demented noises begin to interrupt your thoughts, you struggle through the mental pain and ignore it.<br>\n<br>\nEventually you successfully map out a path forward, and continue on, now resistant to the nefarious nature of this alien place.\n</div> </blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Retrace Your Steps}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou spend what feels like an eternity lost in the maze. Slowly but surely, you are able to retrace your steps, reorient yourself, and make it out of the twisting passages.<br>\n<br>\nYou feel {{TS|red|up|drained}} from the experience.\n</div> </blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Omamori}} can be used to prevent the {{C|Writhe}} from {{Frame|Focus}} if it has any charges remaining. This is likely one of the last opportunities for the player to be able to benefit from {{R|Omamori}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding ambient SFX for Winding Halls event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Winding Hall Event gets a new option and some text improvements. [Retrace Your Steps] Lose HP.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Winding Halls event reworked.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]}}}}